Good Afternoon,

 

Wow!  What a busy day today!

 

Oh, yes....Friday greetings from tropical South Carolina, where we may hit
the 80s today.  Time to break out the shorts!  J

 

Jenny and I are looking forward to a most interesting and colorful weekend
and we hope all of our Joke List friends have an equally wonderful weekend.

 

Our joke today, which may be another recycled oldie, comes from our friends
at A Joke A Day.

 

Keep smiling............ss

 

****************************************************************************
**************************

 

                                                            JURY TRIAL

 

Before a burglary trial, the judge explained to the defendant who had
pleaded not guilty, "You can let me try your case, or you can choose to have
a jury of your peers."

The man thought for a moment. "What are peers?" he asked.

"They're people just like you - your equals."

"Forget it," retorted the defendant. "I don't want to be tried by a bunch of
thieves."

 

 

